1. Adopted code, patterns and prompts
===================================================================================================

Claude Code Agent Monitor — https://github.com/hoangsonww/Claude-Code-Agent-Monitor
Copyright (c) 2026 - Now, Son Nguyen — MIT
Patterns in packages/shared/src/parse/:
- Claude: count token usage only once per message ID (one reply spans several JSONL lines).
- Codex: tokens from the last `token_count.total_token_usage`; cache reads and writes are subtracted from
  input; titles from Codex's own renaming (`session_index.jsonl`).

ccusage — https://github.com/ccusage/ccusage — MIT
- Cost calculation (tokens per type × price per token; cache writes with 1-hour TTL at the higher rate) and
  the price / context-window values follow ccusage (packages/shared/src/usage.ts), checked against real
  `ccusage daily --json` output.

LiteLLM — https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm — MIT
- The price and context-window data come from its dataset `model_prices_and_context_window.json`
  (data values only, no code) — packages/shared/src/usage.ts.

Hermes Agent (Nous Research) — https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent (commit c953b2a)
Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research — MIT
Patterns, prompts and rules translated, shortened and ported to TypeScript:
- apps/server/src/nyx/memory.ts: memory tool with a character budget per area, atomic batches (budget checked
  on the final result), unique-match search, usage display, at most 3 failed attempts per run, frozen prompt
  snapshot (tools/memory_tool.py, tools/memory_tool_store.py, agent/prompt_builder.py build_memory_guidance)
- apps/server/src/nyx/review.ts: prompt and triggers of the background learning review, history summary
  (agent/background_review.py)
- apps/server/src/nyx/sessionSearch.ts: shapes of chat search, relative time filters, down-ranking of automatic
  threads (tools/session_search_tool.py)
- apps/server/src/nyx/todo.ts: task list schema, merge by id, revision, re-injecting open items
  (tools/todo_tool.py)
- apps/server/src/nyx/schedules.ts: cron hint with [SILENT]/[CRON_FAILURE], wake gate, next_run_at before the
  run (cron/scheduler_prompt.py, cron/scheduler.py, tools/cronjob_tools.py)
- apps/server/src/nyx/compaction.ts: clearing tool output, section schema, rolling updates, hand-over prefix,
  emergency summary (agent/context_compressor.py)
- apps/server/src/nyx/speak.ts: Markdown → speech text, spelling out symbols (tools/tts_text_normalize.py),
  adapted for German
- apps/server/src/nyx/threats.ts: threat patterns and invisible characters (tools/threat_patterns.py),
  extended with German forms
- apps/server/src/nyx/prompt.ts: per-turn voice hint (tools/voice_live.py VOICE_LIVE_TURN_NOTE);
  apps/server/src/nyx/tools.ts: tool descriptions
- Personality presets (hermes_cli/personality.py): built-in presets are fixed, custom presets are added
  → `BUILTIN_NYX_PRESETS` in packages/shared/src/nyx-persona.ts and the table `nyx_presets`.
- Skill library (tools/skill_usage.py, tools/skill_ledger.py): usage count per skill, history with SHA-256,
  "pinned" protects from suggestions → packages/shared/src/skills.ts, apps/server/src/skills/usage.ts.
- Learning loop (background_review.py): signals for failed call / cancellation / correction and the writing
  rules for skill jobs, translated → apps/server/src/skills/usage.ts, suggest.ts, jobs.ts. Unlike Hermes,
  NyxOS never changes a skill on its own: suggestions are applied only after the user approves them.
- Telegram (gateway/pairing.py, tools/voice_live.py): pairing code (8 characters without 0/O/1/I, valid 1 h,
  salted SHA-256 hash instead of the code, constant-time comparison, lock after 5 failed attempts, tolerant of
  spaces and case) → apps/server/src/telegram/pairing.ts; per-turn voice hint (translated)
  → apps/server/src/telegram/nyx.ts; approval buttons `<prefix>:<choice>:<id>`, voice mode per chat.

