===================================================================================================
2. Voice container `nyx-voice` (infra/nyx-voice, optional) — dependencies and models
===================================================================================================

Used only as dependencies or model files; no third-party code is copied into this repository.
infra/nyx-voice/nyx_voice/engines.py (`PocketTts`) only calls the public interface of Pocket TTS.

Software

- sherpa-onnx (speech recognition and speech output, Python package, pinned 1.13.8) —
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx — Copyright Xiaomi Corporation and contributors — Apache-2.0.
  The prebuilt model packages come from this project's releases (verified by SHA-256,
  infra/nyx-voice/nyx_voice/catalog.py).
- Kyutai Pocket TTS (Python package `pocket-tts`, pinned 3.3.0) — https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts —
  Copyright Kyutai — MIT. The configuration `german.yaml` from the package is rewritten at start with local
  paths (only the paths are replaced).
- PyTorch (CPU, pinned 2.13.0) — BSD-3-Clause; safetensors, tokenizers, huggingface-hub, sentencepiece —
  Apache-2.0; scipy — BSD-3-Clause; einops, pydantic, pyyaml — MIT; numpy, soundfile — BSD-3-Clause; cffi —
  MIT; pycparser — BSD-3-Clause; other dependencies MIT/BSD/Apache/PSF (full list:
  infra/nyx-voice/requirements.txt and infra/nyx-voice/requirements-pocket.txt).
- GPL components, named openly: they run unmodified inside the container only, are never linked with NyxOS
  code, and NyxOS talks to the service over HTTP only. ffmpeg (Debian package, LGPL/GPL) runs as a separate
  process to convert audio. sherpa-onnx bundles the pronunciation library espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) for Piper
  voices; its data (`espeak-ng-data`) ships with the voice packages.
- Local voice pack (`nyxos voice install`, apps/cli/voice.mjs): nothing of the following is shipped in the
  release — it is downloaded on the user's computer at install time, checked by SHA-256, and run as separate
  programs. uv (pinned release binary) — https://github.com/astral-sh/uv — Astral Software Inc. — MIT OR
  Apache-2.0. Python 3.12 (python-build-standalone, fetched by uv) — PSF License. imageio-ffmpeg (pinned 0.6.0)
  — https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg — BSD-2-Clause; the ffmpeg program it contains is a GPL build
  and only runs as a separate process to convert audio. Package list with hashes:
  infra/nyx-voice/requirements-local.txt.

Models (downloaded into a volume at first start, never part of the image)

- Speech recognition "Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3" — NVIDIA — CC-BY-4.0. Attribution: this model is provided by
  NVIDIA, https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3; ONNX version by sherpa-onnx, unmodified.
- Pocket TTS weights, German, without voice cloning, including the voice "juergen" — Kyutai — CC-BY-4.0.
  Attribution: model by Kyutai, https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning, revision
  4e1e0a3e611c51c0b4ed8174fc10f32a54644303, unmodified, verified by SHA-256. Voice cloning is not used.
- `pocket-en-george`: Pocket TTS weights, English, without voice cloning (languages/english, revision
  4e1e0a3e) — Kyutai — CC-BY-4.0 — https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning. The voice
  "george" is a recording of VCTK speaker p315 — CC-BY-4.0 (Centre for Speech Technology Research, University
  of Edinburgh, https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/3443; overview of voice licenses:
  https://huggingface.co/kyutai/tts-voices). A separate English model, not a multilingual one.
- Piper voices from rhasspy/piper-voices (run through sherpa-onnx, NOT through the GPL package `piper1-gpl`):
  - "thorsten" (de_DE, high/medium) and "thorsten_emotional" (medium, speaker "neutral") — dataset CC0
    (Thorsten-Voice), according to the model cards.
  - "kerstin" (de_DE, low) — dataset CC0 (dataset-voice-kerstin), according to the model card.
  - "ramona" (low) and "eva_k" (x_low) — M-AILABS dataset (BSD-like license, commercial use allowed).
    Attribution: The M-AILABS Speech Dataset,
    https://www.caito.de/2019/01/03/the-m-ailabs-speech-dataset/.
  - `en_US-ljspeech-high` (English fallback voice) — LJSpeech dataset, public domain,
    https://keithito.com/LJ-Speech-Dataset/.
  - Note: the Piper voices were fine-tuned from an English base voice (lessac/ryan).
- Deliberately NOT used: "pavoque" (dataset CC-BY-NC-SA, non-commercial), en_US-ryan (dataset CC-BY-NC-SA),
  en_US-lessac (Blizzard 2013 license, non-commercial), Pocket voices from Expresso/EARS (CC-BY-NC),
  Chatterbox (too slow on CPU).

Own implementations (no third-party code): the pronunciation lexicon and German numbers/times/dates
(nyx_voice/text_de.py), English numbers/times/dates (nyx_voice/text_en.py), and the per-sentence language
choice (nyx_voice/text_lang.py, mirrored by `guessVoiceLanguage` in packages/shared).
